  "diagram_notes": [
    {
      "content": "# Any.Run file analysis\n\n***\n\nThis story will take input from a form with an email and a file to analyse.\n\nIt will upload the file to a sandbox VM in Any.run and run an analysis.\n\nThe story will incrementally check if the analysis has completed, once completed the full analysis will be emailed to the recipient set in the form\n",
      "position": [
        750,
        -15
      ],
      "guid": "d47cf6176bc422fba888407dbefb0bec",
      "width": 290
    },
    {
      "content": "Continues only when ANY.RUN accepts the file and returns HTTP `201 Created` \n",
      "position": [
        0,
        315
      ],
      "guid": "2d30ff3badf811d99d0313e825846120",
      "width": 290
    },
    {
      "content": "Continues only when ANY.RUN report is retrieved and returns HTTP `201 Created` \n",
      "position": [
        765,
        570
      ],
      "guid": "e3d89fd0264a12baf500bab0963771a6",
      "width": 290
    },
    {
      "content": "Task is still running  \n",
      "position": [
        -15,
        735
      ],
      "guid": "b8558093cb977d348dfb71ae4207c524",
      "width": 290
    },
    {
      "content": "Formats the failed or incomplete ANY.RUN report response into a simple status code and message for the error email.\n",
      "position": [
        780,
        720
      ],
      "guid": "120fac24ef93ccead4f19f7ab9a7f460",
      "width": 290
    },
    {
      "content": "Time out\n",
      "position": [
        -30,
        975
      ],
      "guid": "66365810727091fff997395477b9a426",
      "width": 290
    },
    {
      "content": "This playbook accepts suspicious file submissions, sends them to ANY.RUN for sandbox analysis, periodically checks for the analysis result, and emails either the findings or an error outcome.\n\nObjective: automate basic malware-analysis triage by submitting files to ANY.RUN and notifying the user when analysis completes or fails.\n",
      "position": [
        60,
        -135
      ],
      "guid": "8000506bc65f09c71d41aadc471b3e5c",
      "width": 960
    },
    {
      "content": "**Disclaimer**: This is a proof-of-concept playbook and is not production-ready. Before production use, add secure file handling, access controls, input validation, credential management, retry/error handling, monitoring, alerting, rate-limit controls, and organization-approved data-sharing and retention policies.\n",
      "position": [
        60,
        -225
      ],
      "guid": "9cabd4b57d02405ec480043632142873",
      "width": 944
    }
  ],
